    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_41716e0b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a man speaking at a podium with overlaid text that reads: \"i think if people want to wipe out reminders of slavery segregation & white supremacy we might consider getting rid of the democratic party.\" The overall intent is to provoke controversy by suggesting that the Democratic Party, which is historically associated with civil rights and racial justice, should be eliminated if one wishes to erase the historical legacy of slavery, segregation, and white supremacy. This is a harmful and misleading statement because it falsely equates the Democratic Party with the very systems it has historically opposed and sought to dismantle. The meme uses the speaker's image to lend false authority to this inflammatory and historically inaccurate claim, potentially inciting division and misunderstanding about the role of political parties in addressing racial injustice. The intent is to weaponize historical grievances against a political party, which can be seen as a form of political propaganda designed to delegitimize the Democratic Party and encourage polarization. The meme does not contain direct abusive, cyberbullying, misogynistic, or hateful language toward specific individuals or groups, but it is harmful because it promotes a dangerous oversimplification of complex historical and political issues and could be used to justify extremist views or actions.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a738c4a5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
